  "content": {
    "rendered": "\n<div class=\"wp-block-media-text is-stacked-on-mobile\" style=\"grid-template-columns:45% auto\"><figure class=\"wp-block-media-text__media\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"182\" height=\"278\" src=\"https://quranbook.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/04/تحميل-المصحف-كامل-مكتوب-بخط-كبير-pdf-1.jpg\" alt=\"quran karim\" class=\"wp-image-5623 size-full\"/></figure><div class=\"wp-block-media-text__content\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">The righteous predecessors</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> guided by unwavering faith and profound reverence, held the Book of God, the quran karim , in the highest esteem.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> They recognized it as the divine revelation, a masterpiece of unparalleled eloquence and wisdom, far surpassing any human composition. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Their approach to the Quran was characterized by utmost respect and meticulous dedication, reflecting their deep understanding of its significance and transformative power.</p>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">With unwavering devotion</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">they recited the quran karim, savoring each word and pondering over its profound meanings. They delved into its verses, extracting guidance and inspiration for their lives. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Quran&#8217;s beauty and wisdom captivated their hearts, prompting them to reflect on its wonders and marvel at its miraculous nature.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Their commitment to the Quran extended beyond mere recitation. They meticulously examined its verses, discerning the general and specific, the abrogated and non-abrogated, and identifying the signs of its divine authorship. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">They served as ardent defenders of the Quran&#8217;s authenticity, refuting the distortions of extremists and the criticisms of skeptics.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The righteous predecessors never sought to impose their own interpretations or actions upon thequran karim. They understood that true comprehension and adherence to its teachings could only be achieved through careful study and unwavering dedication.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"> As Ibn Masoud eloquently stated, &#8220;If a man among us learned ten verses, he would not go beyond them until he knew their meanings and acted upon them.&#8221;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Similarly, Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami recounted, &#8220;Those who used to recite us told us that if they knew ten verses, they would not leave them behind until they did what was in them, so we learned the Quran and the work together.&#8221;</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The righteous predecessors set an exemplary model for approaching the Quran, demonstrating that true understanding and adherence to its teachings stem from a combination of reverence, study, and action. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Their legacy serves as a perpetual reminder of the profound impact the Quran can have on our lives when approached with the proper mindset and dedication. Their unwavering devotion to the Quran remains a beacon of inspiration for generations to come.</p>\n\n\n<p> <div class=\"quran_gateway_sora_list\"><h2 class=\"sora_title\">The Noble Qur'an</h2><ul><li>1. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=1\">Al-Fatihah ( The Opening )</a></li><li>2. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=2\">Al-Baqarah ( The Cow )</a></li><li>3. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=3\">Al-Imran ( The Famiy of Imran )</a></li><li>4. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=4\">An-Nisa ( The Women )</a></li><li>5. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=5\">Al-Maidah ( The Table spread with Food )</a></li><li>6. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=6\">Al-An'am ( The Cattle )</a></li><li>7. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=7\">Al-A'raf (The Heights )</a></li><li>8. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=8\">Al-Anfal ( The Spoils of War )</a></li><li>9. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=9\">At-Taubah ( The Repentance )</a></li><li>10. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=10\">Yunus ( Jonah )</a></li><li>11. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=11\">Hud</a></li><li>12. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=12\">Yusuf (Joseph )</a></li><li>13. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=13\">Ar-Ra'd ( The Thunder )</a></li><li>14. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=14\">Ibrahim ( Abraham )</a></li><li>15. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=15\">Al-Hijr ( The Rocky Tract )</a></li><li>16. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=16\">An-Nahl ( The Bees )</a></li><li>17. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=17\">Al-Isra ( The Night Journey )</a></li><li>18. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=18\">Al-Kahf ( The Cave )</a></li><li>19. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=19\">Maryam ( Mary )</a></li><li>20. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=20\">Taha</a></li><li>21. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=21\">Al-Anbiya ( The Prophets )</a></li><li>22. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=22\">Al-Hajj ( The Pilgrimage )</a></li><li>23. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/quran-karim/?language_id=1&sora_id=23\">Al-Mu'minoon ( The Believers )</a></li><li>24. <a href=\"https://quranbook.org/q